    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d583">

                <pb facs="0670" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg658"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.248/110: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-12-24T16:00:00+03:25">December 24,
                            1940—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 25—1:14 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>276. Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs<anchor n="52a" xml:id="d583-f1"/>
                    informs me that Iranian Military Mission in the United States has arranged with
                    Curtiss Company for a technical expert now in Australia to come to Iran to study
                    the possibilities of manufacturing pursuit planes in this country with American
                    equipment.</p>
                <p>He stated that the plan now lacks only the authorization of the Department and
                    requested the good offices of the Legation to obtain it. The foregoing is
                    transmitted for the Department’s information and any comment it may wish to
                    make.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d583-f1" n="52a" xml:id="d583-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably the Under Secretary for Foreign Affairs, Djevad Amery.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
